    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Streeting sparks storm"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Streeting sparks storm
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening?</strong> Wes Streeting has <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgkpr6y3266o" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">resigned as health secretary</a> after saying he no longer has confidence in PM Keir Starmer’s leadership. He did not formally launch a leadership challenge, but allies said he has enough MP support to trigger one. Some MPs who are loyal to Starmer still believe he can survive, while Streeting’s allies say they are waiting to see whether Starmer resigns voluntarily or sets a timetable for leaving.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Details:</strong> In his resignation letter, Streeting argued that Starmer would not lead Labour into the next general election and blamed the government’s unpopularity for Labour’s poor election results. Streeting criticised a lack of direction, saying the country needed bold vision and bigger solutions. He said the party needed a broad debate about its future, based on ideas rather than personalities or factional fights.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Big picture: </strong>Streeting’s resignation turns Labour’s internal doubts into an open leadership crisis. Starmer is no longer just facing criticism from opponents but also direct pressure from senior figures within his own party. The row shows Labour is struggling to explain its direction after poor election results, with MPs and unions debating whether Starmer can still lead them into the next general election. Streeting’s move also raises the possibility of a wider contest involving figures such as Angela Rayner or Andy Burnham.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" css-class="border-line" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
