<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Safer streets app"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Safer streets app
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What happened?</strong> An app called Safest Way has been launched to help people <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm2pndkmk0ko" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">find the “safest” walking route home</a>. It is currently available in York, London, and Northern Ireland, with plans to expand across the UK. Co-founder Alesja Gilvear said the idea came after she noticed normal navigation apps did not warn users about poorly lit streets. The app is aimed at anyone who wants more confidence while walking, though most users are currently women.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>How?</strong> The Safest Way app works by combining public and location-based data to rank walking routes by perceived safety. Instead of simply choosing the fastest or shortest route, it considers factors such as street lighting, CCTV coverage, crime statistics, and areas that may feel isolated or risky at night. It requires no registration and is open for use.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Big picture: </strong>The Safest Way app reflects a growing push to treat public safety as part of everyday urban design. Earlier this year, a YouGov poll suggested 88% of women feel unsafe walking alone at night. The app may provide reassurance, but it also highlights the need for better-lit streets, safer public spaces, stronger reporting systems, and wider measures to make cities feel safe for everyone.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
    
    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
